  "primitive_sources": [
    {
      "review": "Primary-source audit of path_openat allocating a file/OFD, may_create write/search checks, may_delete directory/sticky checks and vfs_link directory-hardlink rejection. No Linux code copied.",
      "url": "https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.8/fs/namei.c"
    },
    {
      "review": "The explicit coherent-UID initialized mount profile remains necessary; mount IDs alone do not identify UID permission views.",
      "url": "https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/v6.8/filesystems/idmappings.html"
    }
  ],
  "prior_reviews": {
    "assurance/host-authority-contract-review.json": "7894a8bfe0a5261d95ff9c843a7dfed9965b43e06accba5b85cd71994564a349",
    "assurance/host-marker-custody-review.json": "82f00cc9758d5f16e1a7249486ddb0c0b0874195f6c1c2a77c076c8b9af819ee"
  },
  "review": {
    "caller": "selected_mkdir_site derives a real run/validator creation or publication branch from the actual Entrypoint/packet/CLI source prefix. run_creation_mkdir_authority consumes that actual creation branch and derives the retained parent raw reference, actual host UID, current trusted metadata, reserved component and448 mode. selected_commit_authority derives its parent/container/stage from the same actual parent/fresh/prepare source, proves container aliases parent, and derives current parent UID/metadata for returned/error/lost rename acknowledgements.",
    "foreign": "ForeignAcquisition and ForeignEntryOrigin contain no private/family predicate. They record actual searched parents, lookup permissions, fresh object births, existing nondirectory capabilities, or checked directory rename sources. ForeignNamespaceObservation retains per-operation inserted-binding/lifetime observations. A global ordinary-reference pool includes descriptors and pending lookup/commit references; ordinary copies within it remain possible. O_PATH access to a private root directory is retained, without granting descendant search. No protected_hardlinks sysctl or permission-based revocation of prior writable descriptors is assumed.",
    "foreign_scope": "The per-tick ForeignNamespaceContract records application/owned-child effects separately from ordinary foreign access. The supported primitive effect constructors do not transfer SCM_RIGHTS. Other process memory/descriptor extraction from the host engine/owned children remains outside the initialized threat profile; UID inequality alone does not establish that boundary. Complete actual backend namespace/transfer production and compatible global pool instantiation remain open.",
    "full_statement": "All queried full theorem types and critical structure bodies were reviewed without truncation. Source observations retain actual request/descriptor/UID/metadata arguments, kernel replies, source ordinals and the same global ActorTick positions. No supplied whole SnapshotSafe, PublicationSafe, HostSafe or private-region interval frame occurs.",
    "global_fold": "initial_namespace_custody initializes an empty application family, without assuming that future caller CWDs are initially public. ordinary_namespace_custody constructs the complete ordinary-foreign state transition and preserves every registered peer root. The application/public-path/private-open/cleanup source transition fold is still unfinished; these supporting results are not the complete M5.2 public guarantee.",
    "metadata": "ObservedDirectory and UidSample keep real fstat/euid primitive operations and SourceReturnAt observations. observed_directory_current_authority derives current trust through the exact intervening journal, using OFD continuity and individual external metadata effects. It does not assume that parent metadata or its path remained stable.",
    "mount_profile": "All UID/type/mode reasoning uses the explicitly supported coherent host UID mapping across ordinary bind aliases. Arbitrary idmapped aliases require a later per-mount view model and remain outside this initialized profile. Mount identity observations alone prove no UID mapping.",
    "ofd": "RawReferenceLifetimeContract applies to one raw adapter operation. This ABI has no dup operation and new opens allocate fresh OFD lifetime identities; SDK new_reference remains separate. The derived continuity preserves numeric FD reuse, mutable/shared offsets, initial handoff aliases and lost operations. It is not Linux FD-number injectivity or a whole application descriptor-frame premise.",
    "registry": "register_root_at_commit and register_root_authority_at_commit include committed error/lost mkdir observations. RootBoundaries ties every live family boundary to the same registered birth and derives its trusted-parent authority. State transitions handle descendant/public creation, retained deletion and actual publication effects. Directory authority uses actual mkdir ownership/mode metadata and the same external-step liveness rules, including inode retirement; fixed lifetime type is separate from finite inode-number reuse.",
    "remaining": "Source-derived application family/ownership fold; public root/CWD/path traversal and same birth-to-open/current cleanup link; actual controller/QEMU filesystem footprint; complete key-byte nonexposure and actual key-lifetime signing transcript including persisted reports; compatible joint useful executions and integrated public acceptance."
  },
